{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When a man takes a wife.</b> It too is a connected pericah [lit. 'of a field']." "<b>Favor in his eyes.</b> That she is the opposite of his nature." "<b>And he finds in her.</b> And he cannot expose it, for he has no witnesses. And the sense is like \"or he finds in her,\" just as \"and one who strikes his father and his mother.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "Text witnesses vary between כשרה ('connected/upright') and כשדה ('like a field'); the former is unusual, the latter opaque. Translated hyper-literally; the intended sense is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:34.308122171Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}